# tcc -- in-process C compilation through libtcc.
#
# `zc --cc-mode inproc` uses this instead of running a C compiler as a child
# process. It buys the fast COMPILE only: the result is an executable on
# disk, so the program still runs as its own process and its exit code,
# signals and leaks are observed exactly as before.
#
# libtcc is LOADED at the point of use, never linked. tinycc is LGPL-2.1 and
# this tree is dual MIT/Apache, so dynamic loading is what keeps a binary
# built here out of the combined-work question; `make static-tcc-guard`
# enforces it rather than leaving it to discipline.

# The loader is what needs `dl`. Declaring it here rather than in the build
# means a program that never mentions `tcc` links no `dl`: the reachability
# machinery writes the link line from the units a program actually reaches.
require: unit {
    library: "dl"
}

# available -- can libtcc be loaded from `tccDir` and driven from here?
# For diagnostics, and for a program deciding what to offer. The build path
# does NOT ask: `--cc-mode inproc` never falls back, so it has nothing to
# decide, and asking would make a compile depend on a probe.
available: function {tccDir: StringView} out bool is native

# compileToExe -- compile `csrc` and link it to the executable `exe`.
#
# `tccDir` holds tcc's runtime payload -- libtcc1.a, tcc's own headers, and
# libtcc.so itself. tcc cannot find it alone: the path is fixed when tcc is
# configured, so a relocated one cannot resolve even `stddef.h` until told.
#
# `cflags` is parsed by tcc, in the spelling it accepts on the command line.
# `libs` are the `-l` names the emitted C declared on its own second line.
#
# 0 on success; 1 when tcc rejected the program or the link failed; 127 when
# libtcc could not be loaded -- the code `os.spawn` already uses for "could
# not run the compiler", so a caller reports both through one path.
compileToExe: function {
    csrc: StringView
    exe: StringView
    tccDir: StringView
    release: bool
    cflags: StringView
    libs: (List String).view
} out i32 is native
